      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/drones-hit-ships-in-black-sea-sinking-1-prompting-rescue-operations-126101300481_1.html",
      "description": "Drones struck two ships in the Black Sea off Bulgaria on Tuesday, sinking one and prompting emergency rescue operations, Prime Minister Rumen Radev said.\nRescuers evacuated all 15 crew members from one ship, the Maltese-flagged Chelsea 3, with five receiving treatment for minor injuries, Radev said in a video posted to social media.\nThe crew, which included seven Ukrainian citizens and eight Azerbaijan citizens, reported the ship's deck and hull were hit by three aerial drones.\nOne crew member from the sunken vessel was rescued, Radev added, without providing details about the others aboard. The strikes on the two ships occurred 18 and 17 miles (29 and 27.5 km) from the Bulgarian coast.\nDuring an emergency meeting of Bulgaria's Security Council on Tuesday, Radev called the attacks \"absolutely unacceptable\" and said Bulgaria was seeking NATO and European Union assistance.\nWhile authorities do not possess clear evidence on who was responsible for the drone attacks, \"logic, as I have",
